CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1781651786
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCWhen did the Michael Peters
OL,4,CBBC logo officially launch?
OL,5,
OL,6,FWas it commissioned after Michael
OL,7,FCheckland took over as director-general
OL,8,Fin 1987? Or under his predecessor
OL,9,FAlastair Milne who was sacked in
OL,10,Fcontroversial circumstances?
OL,12,FMore intriguingly, was there always a
OL,13,Flong-term plan to use it on screen
OL,14,Fagain? Or was it initially just meant
OL,15,Fto represent the corporation itself?
OL,17,FAt this time it's worth noting it was
OL,18,Fnot uncommon for individual programmes
OL,19,Fto have their own headed notepaper with
OL,20,Fno corporate branding.
OL,23,APub: 26-Aug-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,200,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13905
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1781651786
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCWhen did the Michael Peters
OL,4,CBBC logo officially launch?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first meaningful on-screen use came
OL,7,Fwith the introduction of the BBC Sport
OL,8,Fanimation at the time of the Seoul
OL,9,FOlympics.
OL,11,FSome regional news programmes also
OL,12,Fstarted to use the new logo.
OL,14,FBut there was clearly no rush to push
OL,15,Fthe logo onto screens.
OL,17,FThe new look Nine o'Clock News launched
OL,18,Fa few weeks after the Olympics ` with
OL,19,Fbold graphics from Lambie-Nairn ` had
OL,20,Fno sign of it but it would have been
OL,21,Feasy enough to add it on.
OL,23,APub: 26-Aug-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,200,120,200,300,0,100
